<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4907] Excessive service instances can be started with dynamic deployment.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4907</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;More than needed service instances can be started when service deployed dynamicly. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For next service configuration all 3 instances will be started even if cluster has 2 ignites nodes only:&lt;br/&gt;
  cfg.setMaxPerNodeCount(1);&lt;br/&gt;
  cfg.setTotalCount(3);&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;See for details: &lt;a href=&quot;http://apache-ignite-users.70518.x6.nabble.com/Ignite-may-start-more-service-instances-per-node-than-maxPerNodeCount-in-case-of-manual-redeploy-td11661.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://apache-ignite-users.70518.x6.nabble.com/Ignite-may-start-more-service-instances-per-node-than-maxPerNodeCount-in-case-of-manual-redeploy-td11661.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
